<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link><description>India News Today: Get latest India news and breaking news from India on Times of India. TOI brings the top news headlines from India on Politics, Elections, Current Affairs and more</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-23T00:03:04+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/-2128936835.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:03:04 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Sonam Wangchuk accuses Centre of betraying Ladakh groups, alleges backtracking on May understanding]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sonam-wangchuk-accuses-centre-of-betraying-ladakh-groups-alleges-backtracking-on-may-understanding/articleshow/135125435.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135125435.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Wangchuk said the representatives of Leh Apex Body (LAB) and Kargil Democratic Alliance (KDA) had come prepared for Oct 22 talks in Delhi as a follow up of the May 15 meeting in Leh, with the expectation that the MHA and Ladakh bodies' respective drafts on contours and powers of UT-level body and district councils, would be discussed.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sonam-wangchuk-accuses-centre-of-betraying-ladakh-groups-alleges-backtracking-on-may-understanding/articleshow/135125435.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sonam-wangchuk-accuses-centre-of-betraying-ladakh-groups-alleges-backtracking-on-may-understanding/articleshow/135125435.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T23:48:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Bharti Jain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135125515,imgsize-102632.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New norms to limit fuel leaks, protect EV batteries in rear-end crashes]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/new-norms-to-limit-fuel-leaks-protect-ev-batteries-in-rear-end-crashes/articleshow/135125137.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135125137.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a notification, road transport ministry has also made the automotive standard, AIS-192, mandatory for Event Data Recorder (EDR) from Oct 2029 if it is installed in any car. The EDR feature is not mandatory for all cars, and it remains an optional feature. EDR records crash details, which help establish what happened immediately before and during a collision. It is similar in purpose to an aircraft’s flight-data recorder.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/new-norms-to-limit-fuel-leaks-protect-ev-batteries-in-rear-end-crashes/articleshow/135125137.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/new-norms-to-limit-fuel-leaks-protect-ev-batteries-in-rear-end-crashes/articleshow/135125137.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T23:36:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dipak K Dash</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135125178,imgsize-237310.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[PM Modi calls for stronger global institutions; takes ‘failed product’ jab at Congress]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-calls-for-stronger-global-institutions-takes-failed-product-jab-at-congress/articleshow/135123081.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135123081.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Prime Minister Narendra Modi emphasized the need for stronger global institutions during his address at the NDTV World Summit. He argued that the current global system struggles to address new challenges, particularly in international relations. Modi also criticized Congress leadership for failing to effectively launch their leader, calling it a burden on the party. Furthermore, he highlighted India's role in international cooperation, especially during the Covid-19 pandemic.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-calls-for-stronger-global-institutions-takes-failed-product-jab-at-congress/articleshow/135123081.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-calls-for-stronger-global-institutions-takes-failed-product-jab-at-congress/articleshow/135123081.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T22:22:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135123312,imgsize-93910.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[CEC impeachment: Speaker Om Birla says fresh motion against Gyanesh Kumar will be examined as per rules]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cec-impeachment-speaker-om-birla-says-fresh-motion-against-gyanesh-kumar-will-be-examined-as-per-rules/articleshow/135122265.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="